<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">José López Portillo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1920–2004</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">José López Portillo was president of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> from 1976 to 1982. Huge oil discoveries in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-of-campeche">Bay of Campeche</a> financed a boom and heavy foreign borrowing under his government, but falling oil prices brought a debt crisis in 1982. He devalued the peso, nationalised the banks and left office as the country entered the 'lost decade' of the 1980s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jose-lopez-portillo.jpg" alt="José López Portillo" width="320" height="451" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dutch National Archives · CC BY-SA 3.0 nl · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jose_Lopez_Portillo_new.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
